Hi,

sorry that it took me so long to reply. I'm terribly busy ATM.

On Wednesday 14 October 2009, Patrick Richardson wrote:
> I'm running rkward-0.5.1 on Ubuntu 9.04. Although I love this program, I
> can't seem to get my scripts to save properly. When I click "Save" I get
> a warning message that the file will be saved as binary. Has anyone else
> had this problem or know how to get rid of it?

This means you have some characters in your file which cannot be represented in 
your current encoding. Often times those are typographic quotes or long 
dashes. Either find those characters and replace them, or switch to UTF-8 
encoding (Edit->Tools Move->Encoding).

Note that the warning message comes from the katepart that we use for the 
editor in RKWard. And yes, this warning could really be more helpful (see also 
https://bugs.kde.org/show_bug.cgi?id=89866).

Regards
Thomas
